linux-zako

Linux-libre with the Zen patchset and the BORE scheduler on top.

Layout
    releases/<tag>/patches/   patch set of that release
    releases/<tag>/series     order to apply them in
    releases/<tag>/sources    base tarball, its URL and sha256, plus the Zen tag
                              and the BORE version it was built against
    COPYING                   GPL-2

    One directory per published tag, kept forever. A new release adds a
    directory, no existing directory is ever rewritten.

Build
    cd releases/<tag>
    tar xf linux-libre-<version>-gnu.tar.xz
    cd linux-<version>
    git apply ../patches/0001-*.patch
    git apply ../patches/0002-*.patch
    make olddefconfig
    make LOCALVERSION=-zako<N>

    Apply in the order given by series. Enable CONFIG_SCHED_BORE in olddefconfig.
    Keep CONFIG_SCHED_ALT (BMQ, PDS) off, it costs cgroup v2 cpu.weight and
    cpu.max, sched_ext and SCHED_CORE.

Tags
    v<version>-zako<N>: kernel version plus a revision of this queue. A new kernel
    version starts at zako1, a Zen or BORE update within the same kernel version
    increments N. Published tags do not move.
